<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Iâl</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Yale</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Iâl, anglicised as Yale, was a medieval commote in north-east <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wales">Wales</a>, around Llanarmon-yn-Iâl and the Alyn valley. Part of Powys Fadog, it passed after the English conquest to the marcher lordship of Bromfield and Yale. The Yale family, whose member Elihu Yale gave his name to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yale-university">Yale University</a>, took its name from the district.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ial.jpg" alt="Iâl" width="320" height="220" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Print_(BM_1878,0511.441).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
